{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvqmrzwCtANbudqL4EGW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018B3pm17mKfmZbSU4GFCp8R","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,datetime\nQ=[\n(\"bribery and margin of victory in voting rules computational complexity\",\"core_method\",\"Minimal targeted boost to make a target rank first is a cost-minimizing manipulation/bribery problem; margin of victory and bribery are the closest formal analogues for the cost-vs-rule comparison (depth L1 cost, breadth cost).\"),\n(\"manipulation of Borda and Copeland rules complexity\",\"core_method\",\"Borda, Copeland and plurality are the rank-based rules solved by MILP level selection; their manipulation/bribery hardness motivates exact vs heuristic solvers.\"),\n(\"rank aggregation of multi-task benchmark scores with social choice rules (Borda, Copeland, maximin)\",\"baseline_comparator\",\"Comparator literature for the aggregation rules studied (mean, median, trimmed mean, min, Borda, plurality, Copeland); beyond starter items 5 and 11, includes Vote'n'Rank-style benchmark aggregation.\"),\n(\"robustness of rankings to task selection and aggregation choice in multi-task benchmarks\",\"baseline_comparator\",\"Reviewers expect connection to benchmark-lottery/task-sensitivity work: how rule choice changes who is first, which is the baseline for the paper's rule-dependence claim.\"),\n(\"trimmed mean median robust location estimator breakdown point\",\"core_method\",\"Mean, median and trimmed mean differ in how many per-task boosts are needed; breakdown point/influence function theory explains the predicted cost ordering.\"),\n(\"benchmark contamination training on test data inflates language model leaderboard scores\",\"result_driven_theme\",\"Targeted investment is modeled as including subset-related data in training; contamination/leakage literature supports the plausibility and magnitude of per-task score gains.\"),\n(\"adaptive overfitting and holdout reuse in machine learning leaderboards\",\"result_driven_theme\",\"Strategic targeting of leaderboard components is a form of overfitting to the evaluation; Ladder/holdout-reuse work frames leaderboard gaming and limits of the claims.\"),\n(\"Open LLM Leaderboard IFEval GPQA MuSR MMLU-Pro BBH MATH benchmark suite\",\"benchmark_context\",\"Scientific context for the 6-task Open LLM Leaderboard data used; the task components need citations.\"),\n(\"HELM MMLU 57 subjects per-subject scores language model evaluation\",\"benchmark_context\",\"57-subject HELM MMLU v1.13.0 is the many-task setting; the dataset and evaluation framework need accurate citations.\"),\n(\"confidence intervals and uncertainty for model rankings on leaderboards bootstrap\",\"result_driven_theme\",\"The run reports bootstrap CIs and subsample-task robustness over rankings; ranking-uncertainty literature supports the methodology.\"),\n]\nplan={\"status\":\"ready\",\n\"central_topic\":\"How much per-task targeted investment (score boost, measured by L1 depth and breadth over subtasks) a developer needs to make a target model rank first on public multi-task leaderboards (HELM MMLU 57 subjects, Open LLM Leaderboard 6 tasks), and how that minimal cost varies across aggregation rules.\",\n\"core_methods\":[\"Minimum-cost boost plan solvers per aggregation rule (exact for mean/median/maximin/plurality; verified heuristics and MILP level selection for trimmed mean/Borda/Copeland/z-score)\",\"Exact-replica verification and verified boundary polishing (bisection shrink, redundant-drop, pairwise transfer) of boost plans\",\"Breadth-constrained cost (number of tasks boosted) vs depth (L1 total boost)\",\"Bootstrap CIs, task-subsampling robustness, Holm/Wilcoxon tests\"],\n\"comparators\":[\"Computational social choice: bribery, margin of victory, manipulation of voting rules\",\"Social-choice aggregation for multi-task/agent evaluation (Vote'n'Rank, Lanctot et al.)\",\"Benchmark-lottery / task-selection sensitivity\",\"Benchmark contamination and leaderboard gaming (Leaderboard Illusion, contamination papers)\",\"Robust statistics (trimmed mean, median breakdown point)\"],\n\"benchmarks\":[\"HELM MMLU v1.13.0 (57 subjects)\",\"Open LLM Leaderboard contents/results (IFEval, BBH, MATH Lvl 5, GPQA, MuSR, MMLU-Pro)\"],\n\"architectural_shifts\":[\"Shift from heuristic per-rule search to exact/verified per-rule solvers, then MILP level selection for rank-based rules, then verified boundary polishing; grounded only in solver design, not in model architecture changes. Modest measured solver-efficiency gains: combined score 1.0018 -> 1.0034, all runs verified correct, plan validity rate 1.0.\"],\n\"result_driven_themes\":[\"Minimal investment depends strongly on aggregation rule (mean vs median vs min vs rank-based rules)\",\"Verified exact/near-exact plans with small gains from polishing over earlier heuristics\",\"Plausibility of targeted gains via data contamination or targeted training\",\"Uncertainty and robustness of conclusions to task subsets and snapshots\"],\n\"queries\":[{\"query\":q,\"category\":c,\"rationale\":r} for q,c,r in Q],\n\"forbidden_query_patterns\":[\"Any query naming or paraphrasing the withheld published paper on this exact research question (title, authors, results), or pages citing/discussing it\",\"Generic: benchmarking, optimization, scientific method, paper writing\",\"Chronology/search-history phrasing (cycles, attempts, incumbent scores)\",\"Model-architecture queries (transformer, scaling) — no architectures are trained\",\"Starter-literature titles already supplied (MMLU, BBH, HELM, Benchmark Lottery, Lanctot, Leaderboard Illusion, Zhou, Yang, lm-eval-harness, Handbook of COMSOC) except to resolve BibTeX\"],\n\"failure_reason\":\"\"}\njson.dump(plan,open('reference_query_plan.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nmd=\"# Reference Query Plan\\n\\n**Central topic.** \"+plan[\"central_topic\"]+\"\\n\\n## Core methods\\n\"+\"\".join(f\"- {x}\\n\" for x in plan[\"core_methods\"])\nmd+=\"\\n## Comparator literatures\\n\"+\"\".join(f\"- {x}\\n\" for x in plan[\"comparators\"])\nmd+=\"\\n## Benchmarks\\n\"+\"\".join(f\"- {x}\\n\" for x in plan[\"benchmarks\"])\nmd+=\"\\n## Shifts visible in the run\\n\"+\"\".join(f\"- {x}\\n\" for x in plan[\"architectural_shifts\"])\nmd+=\"\\n## Result-driven themes\\n\"+\"\".join(f\"- {x}\\n\" for x in plan[\"result_driven_themes\"])\nmd+=\"\\n## Queries\\n\"+\"\".join(f\"{i+1}. `{x['query']}` ({x['category']}) — {x['rationale']}\\n\" for i,x in enumerate(plan[\"queries\"]))\nmd+=\"\\n## Forbidden patterns\\n\"+\"\".join(f\"- {x}\\n\" for x in plan[\"forbidden_query_patterns\"])\nmd+=\"\\n## Notes\\nNo prior references provenance existed. Grounding: paper_data.json shows 3 solver variants, all verified correct (combined 1.0018, 1.0018, 1.0034; final sealed eval ≈1.0026), no ablations directory. Queries stay in social-choice manipulation, benchmark aggregation, contamination, and leaderboard-data context. Generic alternatives (e.g. 'benchmarking', 'optimization') were rejected as non-specific. No retrieval performed.\\n\"\nopen('reference_query_plan.md','w').write(md)\nts=datetime.datetime.utcnow().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')\nnote=f\"\\n- {ts} | step=reference_plan | Wrote 10-query reference plan (bribery/margin of victory, Borda/Copeland manipulation, social-choice benchmark aggregation, task-selection sensitivity, trimmed-mean robustness, contamination, adaptive overfitting, Open LLM/HELM context, ranking uncertainty). Rejected generic benchmarking/optimization queries and anything near the withheld paper.\\n\"\nfor f in ['memory.md','global_memory/memory.md']: open(f,'a').write(note)\nopen('global_memory/memory.jsonl','a').write(json.dumps({\"step\":\"reference_plan\",\"scope\":\"paper\",\"summary\":\"10-query reference plan written; specific to social-choice manipulation, benchmark aggregation, contamination, leaderboard data context; generic queries rejected\",\"timestamp\":ts})+\"\\n\")\nEOF\nls reference_query_plan.*"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3900,"cache_read_input_tokens":28723,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3900},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab3fe65b-e609-4005-8274-e8764df57876","uuid":"dc620586-d30f-4316-90f2-b1a22d5072b3","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:41:31.158Z","request_id":"req_011CgvqmroXXLftiaDkiUUUR"}
